doc:sch-2-sec-35g-ss-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35G(8) Reconsideration of compliance notice" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(8) If the President’s functions under this section are performed by a delegate of the President, the delegate who reconsiders a compliance notice:  (a) must not have been involved in giving the compliance notice; and  Positive duty  Schedule 2 Compliance  Part 2  No. 85, 2022 Anti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment (Respect at Work) Act 2022  (b) must hold a position, or perform duties, of at least the same level as the person who gave the compliance notice." ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35H Review of compliance notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-35h ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person who has been given a compliance notice may apply to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) for a review of the notice on either or both of the following grounds:  (a) the person has not failed to comply as set out in the notice;  (b) the notice does not comply with subsection 35F(2) or (3).  (1A) The application must be made within:  (a) if the compliance notice has been reconsidered under section 35G—21 days after the person was given a notice of a decision under subsection 35G(6) relating to the compliance notice; or  (b) otherwise—21 days after the day the compliance notice was given to the person.  (2) At any time after the application has been made, the court concerned may stay the operation of the notice on the terms and conditions that the court considers appropriate.  (3) The court concerned may confirm, vary or cancel the notice after reviewing it." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person who has been given a compliance notice may apply to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) for a review of the notice on either or both of the following grounds:  (a) the person has not failed to comply as set out in the notice;  (b) the notice does not comply with subsection 35F(2) or (3).  (1A) The application must be made within:  (a) if the compliance notice has been reconsidered under section 35G—21 days after the person was given a notice of a decision under subsection 35G(6) relating to the compliance notice; or  (b) otherwise—21 days after the day the compliance notice was given to the person.  (2) At any time after the application has been made, the court concerned may stay the operation of the notice on the terms and conditions that the court considers appropriate.  (3) The court concerned may confirm, vary or cancel the notice after reviewing it."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2880f2ccdbb3716e83677c41214360725eb0c08df2e62b22bb3ddb889f6179a7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-3 ;
