concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-6-sec-13 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13 Section 13B"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-13 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the section, substitute: 13B  When public reports are due  Unless a relevant employer has received an extension of time in which to lodge a report under section 17:  (a) if the relevant employer is a Commonwealth company or Commonwealth entity—the employer must lodge a public report under section 13A within 2 months after the day  Schedule 6  Amendment of the Workplace Gender Equality Act 2012  Anti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment (Respect at Work) Act 2022 No. 85, 2022  determined by the Agency for the purposes of this paragraph; and  (b) otherwise—the relevant employer must lodge a public report under section 13A within 2 months after the end of the period to which the report relates." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the section, substitute: 13B  When public reports are due  Unless a relevant employer has received an extension of time in which to lodge a report under section 17:  (a) if the relevant employer is a Commonwealth company or Commonwealth entity—the employer must lodge a public report under section 13A within 2 months after the day  Schedule 6  Amendment of the Workplace Gender Equality Act 2012  Anti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment (Respect at Work) Act 2022 No. 85, 2022  determined by the Agency for the purposes of this paragraph; and  (b) otherwise—the relevant employer must lodge a public report under section 13A within 2 months after the end of the period to which the report relates."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "55e867d560de7155e46b597f5239073745fb1a166dfb41c62380f9c36652802a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must lodge a public report under section 13A within 2 months after the end of the period to which the report relates." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
