doc:sch-7-sec-16 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "16 Section 105" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Omit “2 or 3”, substitute “2, 3 or 5”.  Victimisation  Schedule 7 Application and transitional provisions  Part 2  No. 85, 2022 Anti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment (Respect at Work) Act 2022" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-7-sec-17 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17 Application—pre-commencement acts of victimisation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-17 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of subsection 47A(1) of the Age Discrimination Act 2004 (as added by this Schedule):  (a) it is immaterial whether the act was committed before, at or after the commencement of this item; and  (b) so far as that subsection relates to an act committed before the commencement of this item, that subsection is modified by inserting “, and is taken to have been unlawful,” after “unlawful”. (2) For the purposes of subsection 58A(1) of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (as added by this Schedule):  (a) it is immaterial whether the act was committed before, at or after the commencement of this item; and  (b) so far as that subsection relates to an act committed before the commencement of this item, that subsection is modified by inserting “, and is taken to have been unlawful,” after “unlawful”. (3) For the purposes of subsection 18AA(1) of the Racial Discrimination Act 1975 (as added by this Schedule):  (a) it is immaterial whether the act was committed before, at or after the commencement of this item; and  (b) so far as that subsection relates to an act committed before the commencement of this item, that subsection is modified by inserting “, and is taken to have been unlawful,” after “unlawful”." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of subsection 47A(1) of the Age Discrimination Act 2004 (as added by this Schedule):  (a) it is immaterial whether the act was committed before, at or after the commencement of this item; and  (b) so far as that subsection relates to an act committed before the commencement of this item, that subsection is modified by inserting “, and is taken to have been unlawful,” after “unlawful”. (2) For the purposes of subsection 58A(1) of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (as added by this Schedule):  (a) it is immaterial whether the act was committed before, at or after the commencement of this item; and  (b) so far as that subsection relates to an act committed before the commencement of this item, that subsection is modified by inserting “, and is taken to have been unlawful,” after “unlawful”. (3) For the purposes of subsection 18AA(1) of the Racial Discrimination Act 1975 (as added by this Schedule):  (a) it is immaterial whether the act was committed before, at or after the commencement of this item; and  (b) so far as that subsection relates to an act committed before the commencement of this item, that subsection is modified by inserting “, and is taken to have been unlawful,” after “unlawful”."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "44c9f92e501ca5c9e8029f389fc1efb58c28e44f275b024f4ddf3ab71aeaf01b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Acts committed before commencement are treated as unlawful." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
