concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-7-sec-18 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Transitional—pre-commencement acts of victimisation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-18 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Despite the amendments of the definition of unlawful discrimination in subsection 3(1) of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986 made by this Schedule, paragraphs (ca), (d) and (e) of that definition continue to apply, in relation to conduct that was engaged in before the commencement of this item, as if those amendments had not been made.  Schedule 7  Victimisation" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Despite the amendments of the definition of unlawful discrimination in subsection 3(1) of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986 made by this Schedule, paragraphs (ca), (d) and (e) of that definition continue to apply, in relation to conduct that was engaged in before the commencement of this item, as if those amendments had not been made.  Schedule 7  Victimisation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3fd871b331958b949f1c9e113fc97ed71c37cf0014733992e8fc21fdce243893" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Continues previous definition of unlawful discrimination despite amendments." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
